@startuml QVM_Context_Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

title Quantum Virtual Machine (QVM) - Context Diagram

' External Actors
actor "Quantum Algorithm\nDeveloper" as Developer
actor "Educational\nUser" as Student
actor "System\nAdministrator" as Admin

' External Systems
component "Web Browser" as Browser
database "File System" as FileSystem
cloud "External Quantum\nPlatforms\n(IBM Quantum)" as ExternalPlatform

' QVM System Boundary
package "Quantum Virtual Machine (QVM)" as QVM {
  component "QVM Core\nSystem" as Core
}

' Input/Output flows from Developer
Developer --> Core : Circuit Code\n(QASM/JSON)
Developer --> Core : Configuration\nParameters
Core --> Developer : Simulation Results
Core --> Developer : Visualizations
Core --> Developer : Performance Metrics

' Input/Output flows from Student
Student --> Browser : Circuit Input
Browser --> Core : HTTP Requests
Core --> Browser : Results & Visualizations
Browser --> Student : Interactive Display

' Input/Output flows from Admin
Admin --> Core : System Configuration
Core --> Admin : System Metrics\n& Logs

' File System interactions
Core --> FileSystem : Read Circuit Files\n(QASM/JSON)
Core --> FileSystem : Write Results\n(CSV/JSON)
Core --> FileSystem : Export Circuits\n(QASM)
FileSystem --> Core : Circuit Data

' External Platform interactions
Core --> ExternalPlatform : Export QASM\nCircuits
ExternalPlatform --> Core : Circuit Templates\n(Optional)

' Notes
note right of Developer
  Primary user who:
  - Writes quantum algorithms
  - Tests on different architectures
  - Analyzes transpilation results
  - Exports to external platforms
end note

note right of Student
  Educational user who:
  - Learns quantum computing
  - Uses Web GUI for visualization
  - Experiments with circuits
end note

note right of Admin
  System administrator who:
  - Monitors performance
  - Manages configurations
  - Reviews system logs
end note

note bottom of QVM
  **System Boundary:**
  - Accepts: QASM 2.0, QASM 3.0, JSON circuits
  - Processes: Parse, Transpile, Simulate
  - Outputs: Results, Visualizations, Metrics
  - Interfaces: CLI, REST API, Web GUI
end note

note right of FileSystem
  **Supported Formats:**
  Input: .qasm, .json
  Output: .qasm, .json, .csv, .png
end note

note right of ExternalPlatform
  **Interoperability:**
  - OpenQASM 2.0/3.0 standard
  - Compatible with IBM Quantum
  - Enables cloud execution
end note

@enduml
